      "name": "Backdrop",
      "category": "passive",
      "placement": "mid",
      "activity": null,
      "traits": [],
      "entries": [
        "When a creature attempts to Strike a living mural and critically misses, the attacker hits the surface (a wall, canvas, or so on) behind the living mural. This can damage or break the weapon or surface."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Surface-Bound",
      "category": "passive",
      "placement": "mid",
      "activity": null,
      "traits": [],
      "entries": [
        "A living mural can move only along flat surfaces such as floors and walls. This allows it to end its movement wrapped around corners when on a continuous surface. If the surface it's on is destroyed (such as a portrait hit by a fireball spell or a puddle being splashed), the mural takes 10d6 damage and is shunted to the nearest flat surface. If there is no flat surface within 5 feet, the living mural is destroyed."
      ]
    },
